    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d184">

                <pb facs="0399" n="367" sameAs="frus:frus1964-68v28/pg367"/>

                <head>184. Memorandum From James C. Thomson of the National Security Council Staff
                    to the President’s Special Assistant for National Security Affairs
                        (Bundy)<anchor n="1" xml:id="d184-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1965-05-14">May 14, 1965</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item>Laos Conference</item>
                </list>
                <p>You asked about the genesis of State’s new interest in a Laos conference.</p>
                <pb facs="0400" n="368" xml:id="pg368"/>
                <p>The initiative came from Mr. Rusk, who signed off on a circular on May 10th
                        (attached)<anchor n="2" xml:id="d184-f2"/> in which he concluded that since
                    a Cambodia conference was “pretty well out the window”, we might turn our
                    attention to a Laos conference in order to maintain some sort of diplomatic
                    track in Southeast Asia.</p>
                <p>The responses to this cable have been fairly negative for differing reasons—most
                    cogently, because certain addressee posts disagreed that a Cambodia conference
                    was dead. Since then, as you know, the Cambodia business has shown new signs of
                    life.</p>
                <p>State is sending out a new circular today which moves the Laos problem to the
                    back burner and brings the Cambodia one up forward once again.<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d184-f3"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#bold"> Jim </hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d184-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d184-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Johnson Library, National Security File, Country File, Laos, Vol. XV,
                    4/65–1/66. Confidential.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d184-f2" n="2" xml:id="d184-f2-content">
                <p>It was not a circular, but a multiple addressees telegram, see <ref
                        target="#d181">Document 181</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d184-f3" n="3" xml:id="d184-f3-content">
                <p>Circular telegram 2236, May 15. (Department of State, Central Files, POL 27
                    LAOS)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
